        <text><![CDATA[Time is the selected independent variable.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>  </question>  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q03</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q03</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.CHEM.LAB.03</p><p><strong>Stimulus:</strong></p><table><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Time (min)</th><th>Temperature (deg C)</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>22.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>26.5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>31.0</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>35.5</td></tr></table><p><strong>Question:</strong> Why are units needed in the table headings?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They make the table look longer.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Appearance is not the scientific reason for units.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They replace the need for data.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units support data; they do not replace it.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They prove every value is accurate.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units do not prove accuracy by themselves.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[They tell what each number measures.]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Units give meaning to numbers such as minutes and degrees Celsius.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>  </question>  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.CHEM.LAB.03</p><p><strong>Stimulus:</strong></p><table><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Time (min)</th><th>Temperature (deg C)</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>22.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>26.5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>31.0</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>35.5</td></tr></table><p><strong>Question:</strong> Which value would be suspicious if repeated density trials were 1.02, 1.03, and 1.95 g/mL?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[1.95 g/mL]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[1.95 is far from the other two values and should be investigated as a possible outlier.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[1.02 g/mL]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[1.02 is close to 1.03.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[1.03 g/mL]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[1.03 is close to 1.02.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Both 1.02 and 1.03 g/mL]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[The close pair is not suspicious compared with 1.95.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>  </question>  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> CHEM_U01_L04_GP_Q05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.CHEM.LAB.03</p><p><strong>Stimulus:</strong></p><table><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Time (min)</th><th>Temperature (deg C)</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>22.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>26.5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>31.0</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>35.5</td></tr></table><p><strong>Question:</strong> What is uncertainty in measurement?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
